## Summaries

`totalUnits(rows)` from `src/summary.js` returns the total number of units
sold (22 for the report rows). It used to return the sum of the prices
instead (15); that is fixed.

## Revenue per region

`byRegion(rows)` from `src/regions.js` returns the revenue (units times
price) of each region, as an object keyed by region name, in the order the
regions first appear in the rows.

```js
import { rows } from './src/report.js'
import { byRegion } from './src/regions.js'

byRegion(rows)
// { North: 60, South: 17.5 }
```

Values are plain numbers, not rounded or formatted. Region names are used as
written (case-sensitive), and `byRegion([])` returns `{}`.

